@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Security Best Practices in Azure DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to secure your Azure DevOps environment with best practices for access control, compliance, and data protection.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">Why Security is Critical in Azure DevOps?</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps is a powerful platform for managing software development and delivery, but security must be a top priority to protect sensitive data, code, and infrastructure.
            Implementing strong security practices helps prevent unauthorized access, data leaks, and vulnerabilities in the CI/CD pipeline.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/security-overview.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Security Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Ensuring security in Azure DevOps protects your development lifecycle from potential threats.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Key Security Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Key Security Best Practices</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA):</strong> Protect user accounts by requiring MFA for sign-in.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Least Privilege Access:</strong> Assign minimal necessary permissions to users and service accounts.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Repositories:</strong> Use branch policies, commit signing, and access controls for code repositories.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor and Audit Activity:</strong> Regularly review Azure DevOps audit logs for suspicious activity.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Integrate Security Scans:</strong> Automate vulnerability scanning in CI/CD pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Implement Secure Secrets Management:</strong> Use Azure Key Vault to store sensitive credentials securely.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/security-best-practices.jpg" alt="Security Best Practices" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following security best practices helps maintain a secure development environment.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Implementing Secure CI/CD Pipelines -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Implementing Secure CI/CD Pipelines</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Use service connections with restricted permissions for pipeline execution.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Digitally sign artifacts to ensure code integrity before deployment.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Automate security testing with tools like Microsoft Defender for DevOps.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Restrict pipeline access to prevent unauthorized modifications.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Ensure secrets and API keys are not hardcoded in repositories.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/secure-cicd.jpg" alt="Secure CI/CD Pipelines" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Implementing security in CI/CD pipelines enhances code and deployment protection.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Compliance and Governance -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Compliance and Governance</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Follow Compliance Standards:</strong> Ensure adherence to GDPR, ISO 27001, and other security standards.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Policy Enforcement:</strong> Implement Azure DevOps policies to enforce security compliance.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate Security Audits:</strong> Set up automated compliance scans to detect policy violations.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Restrict access based on roles to prevent unauthorized data access.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/compliance-governance.jpg" alt="Compliance and Governance" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Ensuring compliance with industry standards helps maintain security and trust.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Implementing security best practices in Azure DevOps is essential for protecting code, infrastructure, and deployment pipelines.
            By enforcing access controls, securing repositories, and integrating security testing, organizations can enhance their DevOps security posture.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/security-summary.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Security Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Applying security best practices ensures a safe and efficient DevOps workflow.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>